These species vary in habitat, color, and fragrance, contributing to the diversity of the genus Rosa.To care for a rose, choose a sunny spot with well-drained soil. Water deeply once a week, adjusting based on rainfall. Mulch to retain moisture and suppress weeds. Prune in early spring to remove dead or weak growth and shape the plant. Fertilize with a balanced rose food during the growing season. Monitor for pests like aphids and treat with insecticidal soap if needed. Deadhead spent blooms to encourage flowering. Protect roots in winter with mulch, and cover with burlap in harsh climates. Regularly check for diseases, ensuring good air circulation around the plant.[BE] /recognition received: IMG_20251225_145017590_1766649020137.jpg -> d:\DATN_DACS\DATN\DATN\BackEnd\feature\recognition\imageReceive\IMG_20251225_145017590_1766649020137.jpg

